[{"category":"section","location":"#MobiusSphere","page":"Home","text":"Documentation for MobiusSphere.\n\n","title":"MobiusSphere"},{"category":"method","location":"#MobiusSphere.Mobius_to_rigid-Union{Tuple{MobiusTransformation{T}}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{MobiusTransformation{T}, Any}} where T","page":"Home","text":"Mobius_to_rigid(m, source=(0, 1, 2))\n\nGiven a Möbius transformation m returns Q, T (rotation matrix and translation vector) such that m(z) = p_T(Q*p(z)+T), where p = stereo() is the standard stereographic projection and p_T = stereo(T) is the stereo projection centred at T.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MobiusSphere.Mobius_to_rigid"},{"category":"function","location":"#MobiusSphere.rigid_to_Mobius","page":"Home","text":"rigid_to_Mobius(Q, T, source=[0, 1, 1*im])\n\nGiven a 3D rotation Q (Q*Q'=I, det(Q)=1) and a translation vector T, returns the Möbius transformation m defined by m(z) = p_T(Q*p(z)+T).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MobiusSphere.rigid_to_Mobius"}]
